        <obo:IAO_0000115>A type of crystallography evidence where a purified sample at high concentration is crystallised and the crystals are exposed to an x ray beam to obtain three dimensional molecular structure of proteins and biological macromolecules.</obo:IAO_0000115>
        <obo:IAO_0000234>CollecTF</obo:IAO_0000234>
        <oboInOwl:created_by>swolfish</oboInOwl:created_by>
        <oboInOwl:creation_date>2015-11-04T10:56:22Z</oboInOwl:creation_date>
        <oboInOwl:hasOBONamespace>eco</oboInOwl:hasOBONamespace>
        <oboInOwl:id>ECO:0001823</oboInOwl:id>
        <rdfs:comment>X-ray crystallography can be used for a crystal used to probe at the tridimensional structure of proteins. In some cases, it is possible to co-crystallize the protein bound to its DNA binding site, providing detail on the particular arrangement of the two components.</rdfs:comment>
        <rdfs:label>x-ray crystallography evidence</rdfs:label>
    </owl:Class>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/ECO_0001823"/>
