            </owl:Restriction>
        </rdfs:subClassOf>
        <obo:IAO_0000115>A type of patch-clamp recording evidence that involves isolation of a patch of membrane electrically from the external solution and to record current flowing into the patch and this is achieved by pressing a fire-polished glass pipette, which has been filled with a suitable electrolyte solution, against the surface of a cell and applying light suction.</obo:IAO_0000115>
