        <owl:annotatedTarget>OBSOLETE. A type of mutant phenotype evidence used in manual assertion where variations or changes, such as mutations or abnormal levels of the product(s) of a single gene of interest, including non-mutational changes such as inhibition with antibodies or other inhibitors are determined.</owl:annotatedTarget>
