        <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/ECO_0007661"/>
        <obo:IAO_0000112>This evidence type is commonly used when experimental techniques (such as circular dichroism, NMR, limited proteolysis, or other biophysical methods) are combined with computational predictions of intrinsically disordered regions (IDRs) to support assertions about protein disorder or structure.</obo:IAO_0000112>
        <obo:IAO_0000115>A type of combinatorial computational and experimental evidence in which intrinsic disorder prediction evidence and experimental evidence have been used in combination in order to establish the basis for an assertion.</obo:IAO_0000115>
